他们聊到了“以防万一”这个话题。

441
00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:29.180
Well, they get into this conversation about just in case.
对。

442
00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:29.780
Yeah.
霍莉告诉迈克尔，我们可以把招牌存起来而不是卖掉，以防万一。

443
00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:35.860
Holly tells Michael, you know, we can put the sign in storage instead of selling it just in case.
因为他说这东西属于单身汉公寓。

444
00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.980
Because he says it belongs in a bachelor pad.
对。

445
00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:38.500
Yeah.
对。

446
00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:38.900
Yeah.
以防他以后想回到那种生活。

447
00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:40.860
Just in case he wants to go back to that.
迈克尔说他不需要什么“以防万一”。

448
00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.560
Michael says he doesn't have a just in case.
霍莉也是一样。

449
00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:45.100
And neither does Holly.
那真是个非常温馨的时刻。

450
00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:46.660
It's this really sweet moment.
那真是个非常温馨的时刻。

451
00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:52.540
But right at this sweet moment, a woman walks up and asks about a slip and slide.
就在这美好的时刻，一个女人走过来问起滑水道的事。

452
00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:54.560
And Michael tells her to get loSt.
迈克尔让她走开。

453
00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.600
The slip and slide woman was played by Barbara Bennett.
滑水道女人的扮演者是芭芭拉·贝内特。

454
00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.740
And we had to get permission from the slip and slide people.
我们必须获得滑水道厂家的许可。

455
00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:04.060
Meg Shafe had to call the COO of Whammo.
梅格·谢夫不得不给Whammo公司的首席运营官打电话。

456
00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:09.260
And they said, yes, we could both say slip and slide and show a slip and slide.
他们说，可以，我们既可以说滑水道，也可以展示滑水道。

457
00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.660
Thank you, Whammo folks.
谢谢你们，Whammo的朋友们。

458
00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.100
Here's the rest of the stuff at Michael and Holly's table.
这是迈克尔和霍莉桌上剩下的东西。

459
00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:16.200
We have a lobster hat.
有一个龙虾帽。

460
00:22:16.220 --> 00:22:17.800
We have a sombrero.
有一个墨西哥宽边帽。

461
00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:19.460
We have another straw hat.
还有另一顶草帽。

462
00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.380
We have a mini slot machine.
有一个迷你老虎机。

463
00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:23.020
We have a tambourine.
有一个铃鼓。

464
00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:25.040
The slip and slide, like you mentioned.
就像你提到的，那个滑水道。

465
00:22:25.140 --> 00:22:26.260
And a bunch of other board games.
还有一堆其他的桌游。

466
00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:28.400
It looks like one that says shark game.
看起来有一个写着鲨鱼游戏。

467
00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:29.640
I don't know if you guys caught that.
不知道你们有没有注意到。

468
00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:31.660
One that says Margaritaville.
还有一个写着玛格丽塔岛。

469
00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:33.260
Coffee mugs.
咖啡杯。

470
00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:35.920
That St. Paulie girl neon sign.
那个圣保利女孩的霓虹灯招牌。

471
00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:39.160
And of course, the Cracked Plasma TV.
当然，还有那台碎屏等离子电视。

472
00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:42.220
We got a letter from Kaylee N.
我们收到了一封来自凯莉·N的信，

473
00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:42.960
in Indonesia.
她来自印度尼西亚。

474
00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.520
Up a kabar, Kaylee!
你好啊，凯莉！

475
00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:50.900
Who said, I love that you can see the Cracked Plasma TV from the dinner party episode.
她说，我喜欢你们能从晚宴那一集中看到那台碎屏等离子电视。

476
00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:54.420
I would like to applaud the crew for their consistency.
我想为剧组的连贯性鼓掌。

477
00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:56.720
Yes, I thought that was amazing.
是的，我觉得那太棒了。

478
00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:01.280
The next scene after this is Michael calling Holly's dad.
接下来的场景是迈克尔给霍莉的爸爸打电话。

479
00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:03.320
You know, he knows now.
你知道，他现在知道了。

480
00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:04.560
There's no just in case.
没有所谓的以防万一。

481
00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.040
They're both in it to win it.
他们俩都志在必得。

482
00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:07.800
Which, by the way, is what I said to Josh.
顺便说一下，这就是我对乔什说的话。

483
00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:09.780
Have I ever told you this story?
我给你讲过这个故事吗？

484
00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.040
No, you said, I'm in it to win it.
没有，你说的是，我志在必得。

485
00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:13.700
Or you said, I have no just in case.
或者你说，我没有以防万一。

486
00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:18.220
I said, babe, I don't know about you, but I'm in it to win it.
我说，宝贝，我不知道你怎么想，但我志在必得。

487
00:23:18.340 --> 00:23:20.040
And he said, I'm in it to win it.
他说，我志在必得。

488
00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.860
And I said, all right, let's do this.
我说，好吧，那我们就开始吧。

489
00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:25.580
And then a few months later, he proposed to me.
几个月后，他就向我求婚了。

490
00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:30.440
I want to get you like glasses that say in it to win it or something for your anniversary.
我想在你们周年纪念日时送你一副写着志在必得之类的眼镜。

491
00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:31.820
Now that I know this.
既然我知道了这件事。

492
00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:34.920
Anyway, I just thought of that when they were like, no, just in case.
总之，当他们说没有以防万一时，我就想到了这一点。

493
00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:36.480
I was like, I'm in it to win it.
我就想，我志在必得。

494
00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.940
But yes, Michael is very confident now about proposing to Holly.
但没错，迈克尔现在对向霍莉求婚非常有信心。

495
00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:45.280
And he is going to call her dad and ask for her hand in marriage.
他打算给她的父亲打电话，请求他把女儿嫁给自己。

496
00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:49.260
And Jenna, I really felt like we needed to hear how he went about this.
珍娜，我真的觉得我们需要听听他是怎么处理这件事的。

497
00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:49.900
Please.
请吧。

498
00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:51.240
Yes.
好的。

499
00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:52.260
Hello, Mr. Flax.
你好，弗拉克斯先生。

500
00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:53.900
This is Michael Scott, your daughter's boss.
我是迈克尔·斯科特，你女儿的老板。

501
00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:58.420
I am calling because I am going to have to fire your daughter, Holly,
我打电话是因为我不得不解雇你的女儿霍莉，

502
00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:01.060
because she's such a terrible employee.
因为她是个糟糕的员工。

503
00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:02.280
I'm just kidding.
我开玩笑的。

504
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:03.780
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑呢。

505
00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:08.600
I'm actually calling because I'm in love with her.
其实我打电话是因为我爱上她了。

506
00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:09.920
I love your daughter.
我爱你的女儿。

507
00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:11.480
And I have for some time.
而且已经有一段时间了。

508
00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:18.320
And I would like to discuss my intentions with you, which are to ask her to marry me.
我想和你谈谈我的意图，也就是我想向她求婚。

509
00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:21.400
And I was just hoping that you would give me your approval.
我只是希望你能给我你的许可。

510
00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:23.580
And this isn't a joke.
这不是在开玩笑。

511
00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.880
So call me back when you get this.
所以你收到这条留言后给我回个电话。

512
00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:27.600
And I look forward to speaking.
期待与你交谈。

513
00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:28.940
Thank you.
谢谢。

514
00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:33.580
I love the reveal that it was a voice message.
我喜欢这其实是一条语音留言的揭秘。

515
00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:34.120
Yes.
没错。

516
00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:38.380
I just cringe that he is still fake firing people.
他还在假装解雇别人，这让我感到尴尬。

517
00:24:38.620 --> 00:24:40.420
When has that worked for you, Michael?
迈克尔，这招什么时候对你有用过？

518
00:24:40.640 --> 00:24:41.120
Never.
从来没有。

519
00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:42.120
Never.
从来没有。

520
00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:44.100
He cannot get past that bit.
他就是改不掉这个梗。

521
00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:45.740
And he's so tickled by it.
而且他还乐在其中。

522
00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:51.300
But yes, he left all of that on a voicemail, which is another thing that he's done over the years.
但没错，他把这些全留在了语音信箱里，这也是他多年来一直做的事。

523
00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:53.380
He's left really personal stuff.
他留过很多非常私人的内容。

524
00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:53.820
Yes.
是的。

525
00:24:55.260 --> 00:25:08.380
Back at the garage sale, Dwight has come up to Kelly's table and he manages to get a trade of the candle, the used candle, for a book collection,
在旧货甩卖现场，德怀特走到凯莉的摊位前，他成功用那支用过的蜡烛换到了一套书，

526
00:25:08.380 --> 00:25:11.880
for her Helen Fielding and Jennifer Weiner book collection.
换到了她那套海伦·菲尔丁和詹妮弗·韦纳的书籍合集。

527
00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:17.360
By convincing Kelly that this half-used candle will make Ryan jealous.
通过说服凯莉，让她相信这支用了一半的蜡烛会让瑞安嫉妒。

528
00:25:18.140 --> 00:25:21.620
I would like to point out, I think Dwight is playing Apples to Apples here.
我想指出的是，我觉得德怀特在这里玩的是“苹果对苹果”游戏。

529
00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:23.460
What's Apples to Apples?
什么是“苹果对苹果”？

530
00:25:23.580 --> 00:25:25.040
Apples to Apples is a board game.
“苹果对苹果”是一款桌游。

531
00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:25.920
It's fantastic.
非常棒。

532
00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:28.320
And you basically play the player.
你基本上是在玩弄玩家。

533
00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:31.100
You try to guess how you're going to answer, Jenna.
你试着去猜你会怎么回答，珍娜。

534
00:25:31.380 --> 00:25:34.080
And if I guess correctly, then I win.
如果我猜对了，那我就赢了。

535
00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:36.380
And so he's playing the player.
所以他是在玩弄玩家。

536
00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:40.920
So for anyone who doesn't know, Helen Fielding is an English novelist and screenwriter.
对于那些不知道的人，海伦·菲尔丁是一位英国小说家和编剧。

537
00:25:41.140 --> 00:25:43.940
She's best known for creating the Bridget Jones series.
她最出名的作品是创作了《BJ单身日记》系列。

538
00:25:44.360 --> 00:25:49.900
And Jennifer Weiner is an American writer who, among other things, wrote the novel In Her Shoes,
而詹妮弗·韦纳是一位美国作家，她写过小说《偷穿高跟鞋》等作品，

539
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:54.300
which was made into a movie starring Cameron Diaz and Toni Collette and Shirley MacLaine.
这部小说后来被改编成了电影，由卡梅隆·迪亚兹、托妮·科莱特和雪莉·麦克雷恩主演。

540
00:25:54.860 --> 00:26:00.880
And according to Randy, Meg said, we were allowed to verbally reference the books only.
据兰迪说，梅格说我们只被允许口头提及这些书。

541
00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:02.760
We were not allowed to show them.
我们不被允许展示它们。

542
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:03.260
Hmm.
嗯。

543
00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:04.740
There's your clearance report.
这是你的版权许可报告。

544
00:26:04.920 --> 00:26:05.800
So many rules.
规矩真多。

545
00:26:06.200 --> 00:26:08.380
Well, let's talk about what else was on Kelly's table.
好吧，我们来聊聊凯莉桌上还有什么。

546
00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:12.460
It looked like she had a rack of clothes next to her table.
看起来她桌子旁边有个衣架。

547
00:26:12.560 --> 00:26:12.880
Yes.
是的。

548
00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:15.960
What looks to be maybe a statue of Vishnu?
看起来像是个毗湿奴的雕像？

549
00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:17.980
Some type of dragon head?
某种龙头的装饰？

550
00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:19.660
A wooden jewelry box?
一个木制的首饰盒？

551
00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:20.780
An old alarm clock?
一个旧闹钟？

552
00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:22.880
Three handheld fans, Jenna.
三把手持风扇，珍娜。

553
00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:24.960
You would have bought the fans.
你会买那些风扇的。

554
00:26:25.180 --> 00:26:26.600
I would have loved one of those fans.
我本来会很喜欢其中一把风扇的。

555
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.580
It looked like some fabric.
看起来像是某种布料。

556
00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:30.540
A palm reading statue.
一个看手相的雕像。

557
00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:36.300
Then she had two of these, like, plastic table centerpieces, you know, for, like, a party.
然后她还有两个那种塑料制的餐桌摆件，你知道的，就是那种派对用的。

558
00:26:36.460 --> 00:26:36.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

559
00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:40.540
A disco ball and a bunch of miniature glass vases.
一个迪斯科球和一堆迷你玻璃花瓶。

560
00:26:41.180 --> 00:26:43.900
I think I would have bought the most items at Kelly's table.
我觉得我在凯莉的摊位上买的东西会是最多的。

561
00:26:44.500 --> 00:26:46.540
I think I might have found something on the clothing rack.
我觉得我可能会在衣架上发现些什么。

562
00:26:46.700 --> 00:26:50.400
I could imagine going through there and finding a really great, brightly colored blazer.
我能想象自己在那儿翻找，然后发现一件非常棒的亮色西装外套。

563
00:26:50.600 --> 00:26:51.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

564
00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:54.000
I would have taken the book collection that Dwight just took.
我会把德怀特刚才拿走的那套书给买下来。

565
00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:54.340
Yeah.
是啊。

566
00:26:55.240 --> 00:26:56.420
Definitely one of the fans.
绝对会买其中一把风扇。

567
00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:57.740
I don't know.
我不知道。

568
00:26:57.880 --> 00:26:59.180
Maybe the palm reading thing.
也许会买那个看手相的东西。

569
00:26:59.180 --> 00:27:00.280
If I was in a mood.
如果我当时心情好的话。

570
00:27:00.440 --> 00:27:04.260
You know, when you go to a garage sale, sometimes suddenly you're like, I'm a different person.
你知道，当你去逛旧货甩卖时，有时会突然觉得，我变成了另一个人。

571
00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:05.780
I need a palm reading kit.
我需要一套看手相的工具。

572
00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:07.060
You're absolutely right.
你说得太对了。

573
00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:10.720
Because as I look at her table, my first thought was, I have to have that disco ball.
因为当我看着她的摊位时，我的第一个念头就是，我一定要买那个迪斯科球。

574
00:27:10.940 --> 00:27:11.300
Right?
对吧？

575
00:27:11.420 --> 00:27:12.380
What am I doing with that?
我买那个要干什么呢？

576
00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:13.180
Why do you need it?
你为什么需要它？

577
00:27:13.180 --> 00:27:14.240
Where am I putting that?
我要把它放在哪儿呢？

578
00:27:15.380 --> 00:27:17.100
Next up is Kevin's table.
接下来是凯文的摊位。

579
00:27:17.920 --> 00:27:20.100
Andy and Daryl walk up to check out what's there.
安迪和达里尔走过去看看那儿有什么。

580
00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:21.700
And guess what they see?
你猜他们看到了什么？

581
00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:23.160
A board game.
一个桌游。

582
00:27:23.300 --> 00:27:24.360
They really want to play.
他们真的很想玩。

583
00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:25.120
Dallas.
《达拉斯》。

584
00:27:25.760 --> 00:27:26.280
Yes.
没错。

585
00:27:26.680 --> 00:27:29.440
This Dallas board game is real.
这个《达拉斯》桌游是真的。

586
00:27:29.800 --> 00:27:30.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

587
00:27:30.360 --> 00:27:31.480
It was scripted.
这是有剧本的。

588
00:27:31.640 --> 00:27:33.920
And Phil Shea found it on eBay.
而且菲尔·谢伊是在易趣网上找到的。

589
00:27:34.740 --> 00:27:36.060
Here are some details.
这里有一些细节。

590
00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:38.320
It was made in 1980.
它生产于1980年。

591
00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:40.760
It's for ages 12 and up.
适合12岁及以上人群。

592
00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:42.140
Two to seven players.
两到七名玩家。

593
00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:42.900
Two to seven.
两到七个。

594
00:27:43.180 --> 00:27:44.620
Not two to eight.
不是两到八个。

595
00:27:44.920 --> 00:27:45.380
Yeah.
是啊。

596
00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:46.580
What an odd.
真是个奇怪的。

597
00:27:46.900 --> 00:27:47.460
Choice.
选择。

598
00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:48.900
Cut off.
被切断了。

599
00:27:49.740 --> 00:27:52.280
The playing time is around 120 minutes.
游戏时长大约是120分钟。

600
00:27:53.080 --> 00:27:54.200
120 minutes?
120分钟？

601
00:27:54.360 --> 00:27:54.880
Two hours.
两个小时。

602
00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:57.620
It takes a long time to play the Dallas board game.
玩《达拉斯》桌游要花很长时间。

603
00:27:57.700 --> 00:27:58.440
Holy crap.
天哪。

604
00:27:58.900 --> 00:28:00.440
Here's the quote on the box.
这是盒子上的介绍语。

605
00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:06.120
Take on the role of a character from the TV series in a race to amass the most wealth.
扮演电视剧中的角色，在竞赛中积累最多的财富。

606
00:28:06.500 --> 00:28:07.500
That's the idea.
就是这个意思。

607
00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:11.380
Let me tell you, this was the biggest clearance issue for Meg.
我跟你说，这对梅格来说是最大的版权清理难题。

608
00:28:11.980 --> 00:28:12.540
Really?
真的吗？

609
00:28:13.220 --> 00:28:15.320
Because the game had been discontinued.
因为这款游戏已经停产了。

610
00:28:15.480 --> 00:28:16.980
It was not being sold anymore.
它已经不再售卖了。

611
00:28:17.300 --> 00:28:21.640
Oh, so she had to, like, do a lot of hunting to figure out who the heck to reach out to?
哦，所以她得费很大劲去查到底该联系谁？

612
00:28:21.820 --> 00:28:23.840
Yeah, like, who has the rights to this game?
是啊，比如，谁拥有这款游戏的版权？

613
00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:32.980
Well, it was originally made by a company called Yaquinto Publishing, but that company had been sold to Cardamundi,
嗯，它最初是由一家叫Yaquinto Publishing的公司制作的，但那家公司后来被Cardamundi收购了，

614
00:28:33.160 --> 00:28:39.700
who told them that the game was probably commissioned by Laura Martellavision, which is who made the TV show.
他们告诉梅格，这款游戏可能是由制作这部电视剧的Laura Martellavision委托开发的。

615
00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:45.380
And maybe they owned the rights to the game, but Laura Martellavision no longer existed.
也许他们拥有游戏版权，但Laura Martellavision已经不存在了。

616
00:28:45.460 --> 00:28:49.220
It had been absorbed by Warner Brothers and then dissolved.
它被华纳兄弟收购后就解散了。

617
00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:55.180
So, Cardamundi said, we don't know if we have the rights, but sure, use it.
所以Cardamundi说，我们不知道自己是否有版权，但你们尽管用吧。

618
00:28:55.520 --> 00:29:01.160
I was going to say, at that point, can you just say, we'll roll the dice and see if someone comes after us?
我正想说，到了那个地步，是不是只能说，我们碰碰运气，看有没有人来找麻烦？

619
00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:03.440
Yes, I think that's basically what they did.
是的，我觉得他们基本上就是这么做的。

620
00:29:03.440 --> 00:29:07.640
I think this Dallas board game nowadays would be called Succession.
我觉得现在的《达拉斯》桌游应该会叫《继承之战》吧。

621
00:29:08.440 --> 00:29:09.320
Yeah, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

622
00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:12.980
Well, here were the other things at Kevin's table.
嗯，凯文桌上还有其他东西。

623
00:29:13.740 --> 00:29:17.020
Did you guys see the big train set that, like, went through a mountain?
你们看到那个穿过山洞的大火车模型了吗？

624
00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:18.180
Yes, I did.
看到了。

625
00:29:18.940 --> 00:29:21.100
I'm not sure I'm buying anything at Kevin's table.
我不确定我会买凯文桌上的任何东西。

626
00:29:22.240 --> 00:29:23.440
Yeah, it's a tough sell.
是啊，很难推销出去。

627
00:29:23.560 --> 00:29:25.200
I think the board game was the best thing.
我觉得那款桌游是最好的东西。

628
00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:27.920
Yeah, even though it doesn't end up having all the pieces.
是啊，尽管它最后配件都不全了。

629
00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:29.360
Right, or the instructions.
没错，说明书也没了。

630
00:29:30.220 --> 00:29:39.660
Well, Dwight is going to walk by Jim and Pam's table, and he is very surprised to see a packet of Dr. Copperfield's Miracle Legumes.
嗯，德怀特走过吉姆和帕姆的桌子时，看到一包“库珀菲尔德博士的奇迹豆”，非常惊讶。

631
00:29:41.020 --> 00:29:43.020
But Jim won't sell them to Dwight.
但吉姆不肯卖给德怀特。

632
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:44.520
No.
不卖。

633
00:29:44.940 --> 00:29:47.880
Even though he acquired them under mysterious circumstances.
尽管他是通过神秘的方式得到的。

634
00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:49.340
He was in Jamaica.
他在牙买加的时候。

635
00:29:49.860 --> 00:29:50.100
When?
什么时候？

636
00:29:50.280 --> 00:29:50.760
When?
什么时候？

637
00:29:50.960 --> 00:29:51.360
When?
什么时候？

638
00:29:51.540 --> 00:29:55.840
And a guy knew everything about Jim and then sold him these beans.
有个家伙对吉姆了如指掌，然后把这些豆子卖给了他。

639
00:29:55.840 --> 00:29:57.680
And when he turned around, the guy was gone.
等他转过身，那个人就不见了。

640
00:30:00.110 --> 00:30:02.750
Well, there was more to the scene between Dwight and Jim.
嗯，德怀特和吉姆之间的戏份还有更多内容。

641
00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:04.230
It's in the shooting draft.
在拍摄剧本里有。

642
00:30:04.430 --> 00:30:07.350
It's just a small couplet of dialogue, but I thought it was great.
只是一小段对话，但我认为很棒。

643
00:30:07.530 --> 00:30:11.530
Jim is really trying to bait Dwight, right?
吉姆真的在试图诱导德怀特，对吧？

644
00:30:11.930 --> 00:30:14.890
And in the shooting draft, he would have also said this.
在拍摄剧本里，他本还会说这句话。

645
00:30:16.030 --> 00:30:17.490
Pam must have put them out.
肯定是帕姆拿出来的。

646
00:30:17.650 --> 00:30:19.470
She wants them out of the house.
她想把这些东西清理出屋子。

647
00:30:19.610 --> 00:30:20.890
Of course, it was Pam.
果然是帕姆。

648
00:30:21.710 --> 00:30:22.990
Oh, that's good.
哦，那太棒了。

649
00:30:23.270 --> 00:30:23.590
Yeah.
是啊。

650
00:30:24.150 --> 00:30:27.990
And Dwight's like, no, terrible try, you know, and he walks away.
然后德怀特就说，不，这招太烂了，然后走开了。

651
00:30:28.670 --> 00:30:31.130
The next scene, we have Holly back in the annex.
下一场戏，霍莉回到了附楼。

652
00:30:31.310 --> 00:30:32.290
She's at her desk.
她坐在办公桌前。

653
00:30:32.350 --> 00:30:36.270
She's on the phone with her parents because Michael has called.
她正在和父母通电话，因为迈克尔给他们打了电话。

654
00:30:36.290 --> 00:30:37.790
And her mom's like, what is this about?
她妈妈问，这是怎么回事？

655
00:30:38.310 --> 00:30:40.610
And Holly says, wait, can I talk to dad?
霍莉说，等等，我能跟爸爸说话吗？

656
00:30:41.390 --> 00:30:43.470
Jenna, did you hear what her dad said to her?
珍娜，你听到她爸爸对她说了什么吗？

657
00:30:44.130 --> 00:30:45.470
You know I did, Angela.
你知道我听到了，安吉拉。

658
00:30:45.770 --> 00:30:46.830
Oh, my gosh!
天哪！

659
00:30:46.970 --> 00:30:47.790
It was so sweet.
太贴心了。

660
00:30:47.990 --> 00:30:48.890
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

661
00:30:49.050 --> 00:30:50.630
This is how it read in the script.
剧本里是这样写的。

662
00:30:51.670 --> 00:30:53.270
Holly's mom says, yes, here.
霍莉的妈妈说，好的，给你。

663
00:30:53.270 --> 00:30:55.390
And she passes the phone to Holly's dad.
然后她把电话递给了霍莉的爸爸。

664
00:30:55.950 --> 00:30:57.510
Mr. Flax gets on the phone.
弗拉克斯先生接过了电话。

665
00:30:58.350 --> 00:30:58.870
Hollis?
霍利斯？

666
00:30:59.150 --> 00:30:59.970
Hi, Dad.
嗨，爸爸。

667
00:31:00.290 --> 00:31:02.610
There was a program on TV about India.
电视上在播关于印度的节目。

668
00:31:03.150 --> 00:31:03.670
Okay.
好的。

669
00:31:04.030 --> 00:31:05.130
Did you connect with Michael?
你联系上迈克尔了吗？

670
00:31:05.890 --> 00:31:06.410
Hollis.
霍利斯。

671
00:31:06.630 --> 00:31:07.150
Hollis.
霍利斯。

672
00:31:07.390 --> 00:31:08.670
He calls her Hollis.
他叫她霍利斯。

673
00:31:08.850 --> 00:31:11.450
That was what was on her nameplate.
那是她名牌上的名字。

674
00:31:11.710 --> 00:31:12.210
Yeah.
没错。

675
00:31:12.370 --> 00:31:15.990
On her desk in the first episode that she was in.
在她参演的第一集里，她桌上的名牌就是这样。

676
00:31:16.190 --> 00:31:18.550
Yes, and we were like, oh, my gosh, is her name Hollis?
是的，当时我们都在想，天哪，她名字叫霍利斯吗？

677
00:31:18.730 --> 00:31:19.530
It is.
确实是。

678
00:31:19.670 --> 00:31:20.110
It is.
确实是。

679
00:31:20.110 --> 00:31:21.530
And her dad calls her Hollis.
而且她爸爸也叫她霍利斯。

680
00:31:21.750 --> 00:31:25.910
Although I don't know if you noticed, the nameplate that's on her desk in this scene
不过不知道你有没有注意到，这一幕里她桌上的名牌

681
00:31:25.910 --> 00:31:29.870
that's right under her computer monitor says Holly Flax now.
就在她电脑显示器下面，现在写的是霍莉·弗拉克斯。

682
00:31:30.370 --> 00:31:31.710
It doesn't say Hollis.
上面没写霍利斯。

683
00:31:32.430 --> 00:31:34.890
I want to give a little shout out to the voice actors here.
我想在这里特别感谢一下配音演员们。

684
00:31:35.250 --> 00:31:39.650
Holly's mom was voiced by Bonnie Bartlett, and her dad was voiced by John O'Leary.
霍莉的妈妈由邦妮·巴特利特配音，她爸爸由约翰·奥利里配音。

685
00:31:39.990 --> 00:31:45.370
Did you see at 5 minutes and 49 seconds, Jenna, a shot of Holly's Faberge egg?
珍娜，你在5分49秒的时候看到霍莉的法贝热彩蛋的镜头了吗？

686
00:31:45.870 --> 00:31:46.350
Yes.
看到了。

687
00:31:46.430 --> 00:31:48.270
It's right next to her nameplate.
它就在她名牌旁边。

688
00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:48.750
Yeah.
没错。

689
00:31:49.170 --> 00:31:50.130
What is this egg?
这彩蛋是什么来头？

690
00:31:50.190 --> 00:31:50.910
What is this egg?
这彩蛋是什么来头？

691
00:31:51.010 --> 00:31:54.190
She's not selling it at the garage sale, so it's clearly very important to her.
她没有在车库拍卖会上卖掉它，所以这东西对她显然非常重要。

692
00:31:54.530 --> 00:31:58.210
Well, if you notice that Pam wasn't with Jim when Dwight walked up to their table,
嗯，如果你注意到德怀特走到他们桌子旁时帕姆不在吉姆身边，

693
00:31:58.390 --> 00:32:01.210
it's because she's grabbing coffee for them at the caffeine corner.
那是因为她正在咖啡角给他们买咖啡。

694
00:32:01.610 --> 00:32:04.930
She asked, which one is decaf, which really pisses Hank off?
她问哪杯是低因咖啡，这真的让汉克很恼火。

695
00:32:05.410 --> 00:32:09.010
Well, because he clearly doesn't know, and he's going to have to remake the coffees.
因为他显然不知道，而且他得重新做咖啡。

696
00:32:09.030 --> 00:32:09.390
I know.
我知道。

697
00:32:09.390 --> 00:32:11.690
We had a fan question from Natalie F.
我们收到了一位来自德克萨斯州圣安东尼奥的粉丝娜塔莉·F的问题，

698
00:32:11.810 --> 00:32:13.530
in San Antonio, Texas, who said,
她说，

699
00:32:13.530 --> 00:32:30.490
I love when Pam asks Hank which coffee is decaf because it shows how much her character has grown and how much confidence she has gained since the cocktails episode when she had to really challenge herself to take her beer back and ask for a light after she was given the incorrect order.
我喜欢帕姆问汉克哪杯是低因咖啡的桥段，因为它展现了她这个角色成长了多少，以及自从《鸡尾酒》那一集她必须挑战自我去退掉啤酒并要求换成淡啤酒之后，她获得了多少自信。

700
00:32:31.170 --> 00:32:38.490
She really pushed herself in that moment and took so much courage, and now she doesn't even hesitate to make sure she gets what she wants.
那一刻她真的突破了自我，鼓起了巨大的勇气，而现在她甚至毫不犹豫地确保自己得到想要的东西。

701
00:32:39.130 --> 00:32:42.690
Pam's character development is one of the most inspiring things in the series.
帕姆的角色成长是这部剧中最鼓舞人心的部分之一。

702
00:32:42.990 --> 00:32:43.850
Go, Pam.
加油，帕姆。

703
00:32:44.250 --> 00:32:44.670
Aw.
噢。

704
00:32:44.670 --> 00:32:46.110
I just loved that letter.
我特别喜欢那封信。

705
00:32:46.370 --> 00:32:46.930
I do, too.
我也喜欢。

706
00:32:47.010 --> 00:32:48.330
It's such a great observation.
那真是个很棒的观察。

707
00:32:48.630 --> 00:32:49.050
Yes.
没错。

708
00:32:49.350 --> 00:32:52.190
We got another fan question from Rachel P.
我们收到了来自肯塔基州威尔莫尔的瑞秋·P发来的另一个粉丝提问，她说，

709
00:32:52.330 --> 00:32:54.130
in Wilmore, Kentucky, who said,
她说，

710
00:32:54.290 --> 00:32:59.150
I've always noticed in this episode that Pam has started to wear her shirt untucked,
我一直注意到在这一集中，帕姆开始不把衬衫下摆塞进裤子里了，

711
00:32:59.170 --> 00:33:04.750
and that when she orders coffee at Dwight's Caffeine Corner, she asks Hank which one is decaf.
而且当她在德怀特的咖啡角点咖啡时，她问汉克哪一种是低因咖啡。

712
00:33:05.030 --> 00:33:11.630
Is this a hint that Pam is pregnant after her and Jim's Valentine's Day walk at work?
这是否暗示帕姆在和吉姆情人节在公司散步后怀孕了？

713
00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:20.530
I know that Jenna announced her pregnancy back in May of 2011, and this episode aired in March of 2011.
我知道珍娜是在2011年5月宣布怀孕的，而这一集是在2011年3月播出的。

714
00:33:21.030 --> 00:33:25.670
I was just wondering, is the decaf coffee for Pam or Jenna?
我只是想问，那杯低因咖啡是给帕姆喝的，还是给珍娜喝的？

715
00:33:27.270 --> 00:33:35.630
Well, Rachel, I was pregnant when we were shooting this episode, and I had to untuck my shirt so that no one could see my little growing belly.
嗯，瑞秋，拍这一集的时候我确实怀孕了，我不得不把衬衫下摆拉出来，这样就没人能看到我日益隆起的小肚子了。

716
00:33:35.850 --> 00:33:36.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

717
00:33:36.290 --> 00:33:43.690
And also, no one knew I was pregnant, so all of a sudden, I just stopped tucking in Pam's shirt starting this week.
而且当时没人知道我怀孕了，所以从这周开始，我突然就不再把帕姆的衬衫下摆塞进去了。

718
00:33:44.150 --> 00:33:47.250
Not only did you do that, but we've shared this before.
你不仅这么做了，我们之前也分享过这件事。

719
00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:54.690
You just went and started buying your own shirts to look like Pam's shirts so that people wouldn't know you were going up a size.
你直接去买了和你戏里穿的衬衫一样的衣服，这样大家就不会发现你尺码变大了。

720
00:33:54.690 --> 00:34:01.690
Yes, at a certain point, untucking my shirt, and I had been, like, not zipping my skirt up all the way.
是的，到了一定阶段，我不塞衬衫下摆，而且我当时甚至没法把裙子的拉链完全拉上。

721
00:34:01.750 --> 00:34:02.470
I was sort of, like—
我当时差不多是——

722
00:34:02.470 --> 00:34:03.370
Safety pinning it.
用别针别着。

723
00:34:03.450 --> 00:34:07.210
Yeah, I was using a safety pin attached to a hair tie.
对，我用了一个别针连着一根发圈。

724
00:34:07.330 --> 00:34:08.950
Yes, I showed you that move.
没错，那招还是我教你的。

725
00:34:10.810 --> 00:34:19.110
And eventually, these two tricks weren't working, and I went out one weekend, and I just bought myself a whole new outfit at J.Crew, and I insisted that I had to wear it.
最后，这两个小技巧都不管用了，那个周末我出去逛街，在J.Crew给自己买了一整套新衣服，我坚持说我必须穿这套。

726
00:34:19.110 --> 00:34:23.290
This is what Pam would wear this episode, because if you do a fitting—
我说这是帕姆在这一集里会穿的衣服，因为如果你去试装——

727
00:34:23.290 --> 00:34:24.070
They know.
他们会知道的。

728
00:34:24.210 --> 00:34:25.170
They measure you.
他们会给你量尺寸。

729
00:34:25.290 --> 00:34:25.610
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

730
00:34:25.610 --> 00:34:26.530
In your undies.
只穿着内衣裤量。

731
00:34:26.630 --> 00:34:26.950
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

732
00:34:27.130 --> 00:34:35.150
And they're going to see the belly, and they're also going to be like, oh, yeah, wow, Jenna, you're totally pregnant, and I didn't want to tell people yet.
他们肯定会看到肚子，而且他们会说，噢，天哪，珍娜，你怀孕了，但我当时还不想告诉大家。

733
00:34:35.510 --> 00:34:38.950
So, this was the beginning of my pregnancy hide.
所以，这就是我开始隐藏怀孕的开端。

734
00:34:38.950 --> 00:34:40.550
Rachel, you totally noticed it.
瑞秋，你完全注意到了。

735
00:34:40.570 --> 00:34:41.810
Totally caught that, Rachel.
完全被你发现了，瑞秋。

736
00:34:41.810 --> 00:34:49.430
Rachel, Michael is prepping for his big proposal, which I guess includes a bunch of gasoline that he's pouring around cars.
瑞秋，迈克尔当时正在为他的盛大求婚做准备，我猜这包括他在车周围倒的一大堆汽油。

737
00:34:50.590 --> 00:34:54.790
Maybe he's spelling out, will you marry me, and gasoline, and then he's going to torch it.
也许他是想用汽油拼出“你愿意嫁给我吗”，然后点火烧掉。

738
00:34:54.890 --> 00:34:57.890
We don't know, because thankfully, Pam stops this.
我们不知道，因为谢天谢地，帕姆阻止了这一切。

739
00:34:58.710 --> 00:34:59.030
Yes.
没错。

740
00:34:59.270 --> 00:35:01.330
Hopefully, you all know that was not gasoline.
希望你们都知道那不是汽油。

741
00:35:01.330 --> 00:35:02.670
That was just water.
那只是水。

742
00:35:02.970 --> 00:35:05.830
But I loved doing this scene.
但我很喜欢拍这场戏。

743
00:35:05.830 --> 00:35:13.050
And I had a very hard time not laughing, because the way Steve was performing Michael, so earneSt.
我当时忍笑忍得非常辛苦，因为史蒂夫演绎迈克尔的方式，太真诚了。

744
00:35:13.350 --> 00:35:14.550
So earneSt.
太真诚了。

745
00:35:15.050 --> 00:35:17.790
And I have to say, I really love where this ends up going.
我必须说，我真的很喜欢这个情节的最终走向。

746
00:35:18.130 --> 00:35:19.110
Oh, I did, too.
噢，我也喜欢。

747
00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:24.230
Well, I guess if you want any pesto or salsa, you better head over to Ryan's table.
好吧，我想如果你想要青酱或莎莎酱，你最好去瑞安的桌子那边看看。

748
00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:31.290
He is selling Mama Sally's homemade pesto and Senor Chico's hot cha-cha salsa.
他在卖莎莉妈妈自制青酱和奇科先生热辣恰恰莎莎酱。

749
00:35:31.290 --> 00:35:38.510
Yes, the pesto has a photo of Phyllis on it, and the salsa has a picture of Oscar.
没错，青酱上印着菲利斯的照片，莎莎酱上印着奥斯卡的头像。

750
00:35:38.870 --> 00:35:45.710
He has a talking head where he explains that his mom makes the best pesto, but she would never sell it, even though she'd make a fortune.
他有一个单人访谈，解释说他妈妈做的青酱是最好吃的，但她从不肯卖，尽管她本可以靠这个发大财。

751
00:35:45.870 --> 00:35:48.650
So he decided, f*** it, he'll sell it.
所以他决定，去他的，他要把它卖了。

752
00:35:48.990 --> 00:35:56.530
He tricked her into making him hundreds of jars of pesto by telling her he was going to have a pesto party for his friends.
他骗她说要为朋友举办一场青酱派对，让她帮他做了几百罐青酱。

753
00:35:57.170 --> 00:36:01.310
And Phyllis just kind of looked like the mom he wanted for the jar.
而菲利斯看起来就像他想要的那种适合装进罐子里的妈妈。

754
00:36:01.710 --> 00:36:09.050
When Ryan says, and my mom was like, oh, okay, in the shooting draft it says, said in like a dumb voice.
当瑞安说“我妈当时就说，哦，好吧”时，拍摄剧本里写的是“用一种愚蠢的声音说”。

755
00:36:10.970 --> 00:36:17.510
I am sure you can imagine that this talking head created a back and forth with good old standards and practices.
我敢肯定你能想象到，这个采访镜头在老派的审查标准下引发了一番来回拉锯。

756
00:36:18.110 --> 00:36:19.030
Lip flap.
口型。

757
00:36:19.030 --> 00:36:29.310
Yep, we got a bleep, Ryan's s***, completely with no beginning or end consonant sounds, blur the visible lip flap, or stage this.
没错，我们被消音了，瑞安说的“狗屎”，完全没有开头或结尾的辅音，得模糊掉可见的口型，或者把这一段移出镜头。

758
00:36:29.570 --> 00:36:33.950
My favorite is when they say, the third option is stage this off camera.
我最喜欢的是他们说“第三个选择是把这一段移出镜头”。

759
00:36:34.250 --> 00:36:36.930
Stage a talking head off camera.
把采访镜头移出镜头。

760
00:36:37.030 --> 00:36:38.090
What is the camera on?
那摄像机在拍什么？

761
00:36:38.450 --> 00:36:41.070
What's the camera looking at if he's off camera?
如果他不在镜头里，摄像机在看什么？

762
00:36:41.250 --> 00:36:41.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

763
00:36:41.870 --> 00:36:48.770
So, and then, of course, we turned it in and we got a, as previously noted, blur that lip flap.
所以，当然了，我们交上去之后，正如之前提到的，收到了“模糊掉那个口型”的反馈。

764
00:36:50.050 --> 00:36:53.190
Dwight is still making his trades and his next target is Ryan.
德怀特还在进行他的交易，他的下一个目标是瑞安。

765
00:36:53.610 --> 00:36:59.450
Yes, he explains in a talking head that he traded his thumbtack for Meredith's candle.
是的，他在采访中解释说，他用图钉换了梅雷迪斯的蜡烛。

766
00:37:00.150 --> 00:37:07.330
Then he traded the candle for Kelly's crap, which he traded for Phyllis's garbage, for Oscar's trash, for Stanley's crap.
然后他用蜡烛换了凯莉的破烂，又换了菲利斯的垃圾，再换了奥斯卡的废品，最后换了斯坦利的破烂。

767
00:37:07.610 --> 00:37:15.250
What he got from Stanley was an old photo album, and he's going to trade that with Ryan in order to, I guess, get some pesto.
他从斯坦利那里换到的是一本旧相册，他打算用它跟瑞安交易，我猜是为了换点青酱。

768
00:37:15.710 --> 00:37:16.230
Yeah.
是啊。

769
00:37:16.510 --> 00:37:22.490
That's going to eventually lead him to getting something from Creed and finally a really cute squid that Aaron had.
这最终会让他从克里德那里得到东西，最后还能换到亚伦拥有的那个非常可爱的鱿鱼。

770
00:37:22.750 --> 00:37:28.750
You know, Jenna, at 8 minutes and 31 seconds during Dwight's talking head where he's listing all of the trades he made.
你知道吗，珍娜，在8分31秒，德怀特列举他所做交易的采访镜头里。

771
00:37:28.750 --> 00:37:29.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

772
00:37:29.390 --> 00:37:35.770
You can see in the background that both Phyllis and Aaron have wooden spice racks on their tables.
你可以看到背景里菲利斯和亚伦的桌子上都有木制的调料架。

773
00:37:36.230 --> 00:37:36.830
Really?
真的吗？

774
00:37:37.130 --> 00:37:37.450
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

775
00:37:37.850 --> 00:37:44.710
Well, there was a scene that got deleted where Phyllis is not happy that Aaron is selling the same things that she is.
嗯，有一个被删减的场景，菲利斯对亚伦卖和她一样的东西感到很不高兴。

776
00:37:45.110 --> 00:37:46.550
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

777
00:37:46.810 --> 00:37:48.810
Phyllis is so perfectly annoyed.
菲利斯那种被冒犯的样子真是太到位了。

778
00:37:49.150 --> 00:37:50.270
This is how it read.
剧本是这样写的。

779
00:37:50.550 --> 00:37:54.110
Aaron sits at her table, which has a spice rack labeled $10.
亚伦坐在她的桌子旁，桌上放着一个标价10美元的调料架。

780
00:37:54.110 --> 00:38:02.130
She looks over to Phyllis's table, where Phyllis is setting up the same exact spice rack offered at the same amount of money.
她看向菲利斯的桌子，菲利斯正在摆放完全一样的调料架，标价也是一样的。

781
00:38:02.790 --> 00:38:04.190
Aaron looks to Phyllis.
亚伦看向菲利斯。

782
00:38:04.370 --> 00:38:06.390
Looks like we're in the spice district.
看来我们进入调料区了。

783
00:38:06.710 --> 00:38:07.310
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

784
00:38:07.710 --> 00:38:08.310
Tightly.
紧绷地。

785
00:38:08.710 --> 00:38:09.290
Yep.
没错。

786
00:38:11.730 --> 00:38:20.930
And then later in the episode, you see Aaron slashing the price of hers to $9 to try to undermine Phyllis.
后来在这一集里，你会看到亚伦把她的价格降到了9美元，试图压过菲利斯。

787
00:38:22.570 --> 00:38:27.290
Well, now Dwight is going to return to Jim's table, and the beans are still there.
好了，现在德怀特要回到吉姆的桌子旁了，豆子还在那儿。

788
00:38:27.790 --> 00:38:27.990
Yeah.
是啊。

789
00:38:28.790 --> 00:38:30.450
Professor Copperfield's Miracle Legumes.
库珀菲尔德教授的奇迹豆荚。

790
00:38:30.610 --> 00:38:31.850
Jim's going to destroy them.
吉姆要毁掉它们。

791
00:38:31.970 --> 00:38:32.850
He has had it.
他受够了。

792
00:38:32.930 --> 00:38:33.810
He crumples them up.
他把它们揉成一团。

793
00:38:33.910 --> 00:38:35.130
He stomps on them.
他踩在上面。

794
00:38:35.370 --> 00:38:37.210
He's going to throw them in the trash.
他要把它们扔进垃圾桶。

795
00:38:37.390 --> 00:38:40.170
Let's talk about what else is on Jim and Pam's table for a second.
我们来聊聊吉姆和帕姆桌上还有什么吧。

796
00:38:40.390 --> 00:38:40.790
Please.
请讲。

797
00:38:41.130 --> 00:38:43.810
It looks like a glass lamp fixture.
看起来像个玻璃灯罩。

798
00:38:44.290 --> 00:38:44.450
Yeah.
是啊。

799
00:38:44.450 --> 00:38:45.350
Just the top of a lamp.
只是灯的顶部。

800
00:38:45.630 --> 00:38:46.290
Oh, no, no.
哦，不，不。

801
00:38:46.430 --> 00:38:48.510
That's, you know, the thing that you hang from the ceiling.
就是那个，你知道的，挂在天花板上的东西。

802
00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:48.890
Was it?
是吗？

803
00:38:48.970 --> 00:38:49.770
I wasn't sure.
我不确定。

804
00:38:49.910 --> 00:38:50.530
A hundred percent.
百分之百确定。

805
00:38:50.530 --> 00:38:52.750
I swear I had one of those in my house growing up.
我发誓我小时候家里也有一个。

806
00:38:52.750 --> 00:38:52.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

807
00:38:52.930 --> 00:38:54.470
It was over our breakfast table.
它就在我们的餐桌上方。

808
00:38:54.570 --> 00:38:54.770
Right.
对。

809
00:38:54.950 --> 00:38:55.950
In your breakfast nook.
在你们的早餐角。

810
00:38:56.030 --> 00:38:56.150
Yes.
是的。

811
00:38:56.150 --> 00:38:56.270
Okay.
好吧。

812
00:38:56.290 --> 00:39:03.170
So we have the glass lamp fixture, a bike helmet, golf clubs, a bird feeder, a big green ball.
所以我们有玻璃灯具、自行车头盔、高尔夫球杆、喂鸟器、一个绿色大球。

813
00:39:03.310 --> 00:39:04.510
What is that big green ball?
那个绿色大球是什么？

814
00:39:04.610 --> 00:39:04.970
I don't know.
我不知道。

815
00:39:05.610 --> 00:39:06.050
Legumes.
豆类植物。

816
00:39:06.530 --> 00:39:09.430
Did you catch Jim and Pam's clown painting?
你注意到吉姆和帕姆的小丑画了吗？

817
00:39:09.850 --> 00:39:10.670
Yes, I did.
注意到了。

818
00:39:10.670 --> 00:39:13.750
We also got a fan catch from Haley W.
我们还收到了一位来自北卡罗来纳州夏洛特的粉丝海莉·W的来信，她说，吉姆和帕姆还有

819
00:39:13.950 --> 00:39:19.230
in Charlotte, North Carolina, who said, Jim and Pam also have
一些小丑雕像在出售。

820
00:39:19.230 --> 00:39:21.450
some clown figurines for sale.
而且它们真的很诡异。

821
00:39:21.670 --> 00:39:23.050
And they're really creepy.
它们个头很小，还排成一排堆在一起。

822
00:39:23.410 --> 00:39:26.170
They're little and they're all stacked in a row.
是啊。

823
00:39:26.490 --> 00:39:26.870
Yeah.
海莉问，吉姆的父母也有诡异的小丑雕像吗？

824
00:39:27.310 --> 00:39:31.750
Haley said, did Jim's parents also have creepy clown figurines?
如果是的话，为什么吉姆的父母会对小丑如此着迷？

825
00:39:31.890 --> 00:39:35.570
And if so, why are Jim's parents obsessed with clowns?
还有为什么吉姆和帕姆留着这些东西这么久？

826
00:39:35.570 --> 00:39:39.330
And why did Jim and Pam keep these for so long?
他们住在这个房子里已经有一段时间了吧？

827
00:39:39.570 --> 00:39:42.130
Haven't they been living this house for a while now?
我有太多疑问了。

828
00:39:42.130 --> 00:39:43.530
I have so many questions.
也许他父母对小丑的这种执念解释了他为什么非要捉弄德怀特。

829
00:39:43.950 --> 00:39:48.990
Maybe this clown obsession of his parents explains why he has to prank Dwight.
这很有深度，安吉拉。

830
00:39:49.530 --> 00:39:50.630
That's deep, Angela.
我知道。

831
00:39:50.810 --> 00:39:51.170
I know.
我觉得这应该是吉姆会在心理咨询中谈论的事情。

832
00:39:51.590 --> 00:39:54.730
I feel like that would be something Jim would talk about in his therapy.
我是说，也许他父母从小就用诡异的小丑来捉弄他。

833
00:39:55.570 --> 00:40:00.070
I mean, maybe his parents pranked him his whole life with creepy clowns.
安吉拉，你会从吉姆和帕姆的桌子上买什么吗？

834
00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:03.510
What would you buy from Jim and Pam's table, Angela?
什么都行？

835
00:40:03.710 --> 00:40:04.070
Anything?
别这样。

836
00:40:04.310 --> 00:40:04.360
Come on.
来吧。

837
00:40:04.490 --> 00:40:05.110
Come on.
你在跟谁说话？

838
00:40:05.570 --> 00:40:06.670
Who are you talking to?
什么？

839
00:40:06.890 --> 00:40:07.370
What?
喂鸟器。

840
00:40:07.550 --> 00:40:08.230
A bird feeder.
噢，对，那是真的。

841
00:40:08.490 --> 00:40:09.490
Oh, yeah, that's true.
当然。

842
00:40:09.490 --> 00:40:10.110
Of course.
我在想什么呢？

843
00:40:10.130 --> 00:40:10.890
What am I thinking?
你在想什么？

844
00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:11.710
What are you thinking?
你会拿走什么？

845
00:40:11.930 --> 00:40:12.850
What would you take?
什么都不会。

846
00:40:13.490 --> 00:40:13.830
Nothing.
我是说，这是第一次，我真的什么都不想要这张桌子上的东西。

847
00:40:14.070 --> 00:40:18.830
I mean, for the first time, I don't want anything from this table, really.
也许，也许我会买一个诡异的小丑雕像，然后把它包起来当作“白象”礼物送出去。

848
00:40:19.950 --> 00:40:25.910
Maybe, maybe I would buy a creepy clown figurine and then I would wrap it up as a white elephant gift.
这就对了。

849
00:40:26.250 --> 00:40:27.070
There you go.
帕姆现在要去邀请迈克尔去会议室开会，他刚才叫她了。

850
00:40:27.770 --> 00:40:31.950
Pam is now going to invite Michael to the conference room for a meeting, he called.
好的。

851
00:40:32.090 --> 00:40:33.830
But he doesn't remember calling any meeting.
但他根本不记得自己召集过什么会议。

852
00:40:33.830 --> 00:40:39.810
My favorite thing is when he walks in the room and he's like, hey, everybody, I just wanted to talk to you.
我最喜欢的一点是，他走进房间时会说，嘿，各位，我只是想和大家聊聊。

853
00:40:39.930 --> 00:40:41.010
We're going to talk about recycling.
我们要谈谈回收利用的事。

854
00:40:41.270 --> 00:40:42.250
And Pam's like, Michael.
然后帕姆就会说，迈克尔。

855
00:40:42.410 --> 00:40:42.630
Michael.
迈克尔。

856
00:40:42.930 --> 00:40:46.050
He just went right into some, like, schtick.
他直接就开始表演那一套把戏了。

857
00:40:47.010 --> 00:40:49.890
Pam is going to start to say to Michael, so look, about this proposal.
帕姆正要对迈克尔说，听着，关于这个求婚计划。

858
00:40:49.890 --> 00:40:50.750
He's like, no, no, no.
他却说，不，不，不。

859
00:40:50.750 --> 00:40:52.370
You will not talk me out of this.
你休想劝我放弃。

860
00:40:52.490 --> 00:40:54.710
And Pam's like, she's perfect for you.
帕姆说，她真的很适合你。

861
00:40:54.870 --> 00:40:56.750
Oscar says she's the one.
奥斯卡也说她就是那个对的人。

862
00:40:57.350 --> 00:41:00.030
Jim and Ryan, they're all like, she's amazing.
吉姆和瑞安他们都说，她太棒了。

863
00:41:00.810 --> 00:41:09.970
And Pam explains they just want to help him with the proposal to make it safe and responsible and realistic and doable.
帕姆解释说，他们只是想帮他策划求婚，让过程变得稳妥、负责、现实且可行。

864
00:41:12.490 --> 00:41:15.250
And Michael says, I had a great idea until you ruined it.
迈克尔却说，本来我的点子很棒，直到被你们毁了。

865
00:41:15.350 --> 00:41:18.030
And then Oscar has this speech, and I loved it so much.
然后奥斯卡发表了一段演讲，我特别喜欢。

866
00:41:18.130 --> 00:41:20.290
Oscar says, here's how you do it.
奥斯卡说，你应该这样做。

867
00:41:20.550 --> 00:41:21.830
You take her out to dinner.
带她出去吃顿晚餐。

868
00:41:22.150 --> 00:41:23.350
Go down on one knee.
单膝跪地。

869
00:41:23.510 --> 00:41:26.230
If you're in costume, you did something wrong.
如果你还穿着戏服，那你肯定搞错了。

870
00:41:26.590 --> 00:41:31.650
If at any point you find yourself tying a ring to a dog's collar, stop and look at yourself.
如果任何时候你发现自己正把戒指系在狗项圈上，停下来，好好审视一下自己。

871
00:41:34.090 --> 00:41:36.430
We had a fan question from Carrie B.
我们收到一个来自明尼苏达州凯莉·B的粉丝提问。

872
00:41:36.710 --> 00:41:45.410
in Minnesota, who asked, in the conference room scene where Michael is figuring out how to propose to Holly, who decided which actors got to be in the room?
她问，在会议室里迈克尔构思如何向霍莉求婚的那场戏中，是谁决定了哪些演员可以留在房间里？

873
00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:49.810
Ryan seemed like an odd choice given his not-so-great history with Michael.
考虑到瑞安和迈克尔之间不太愉快的过往，选他似乎有点奇怪。

874
00:41:50.530 --> 00:42:02.030
Well, Carrie, the idea here was that Pam chose who would be in the room based on who would help her achieve her goal of this safe, doable, realistic proposal.
嗯，凯莉，这里的设定是帕姆挑选了房间里的人，因为这些人能帮她实现目标，即策划一场稳妥、可行且现实的求婚。

875
00:42:02.530 --> 00:42:09.450
So I think she picked Jim and Oscar because they are the most level-headed thinkers.
所以我认为她选了吉姆和奥斯卡，因为他们是最冷静理智的思考者。

876
00:42:09.950 --> 00:42:14.790
And I think she picked Ryan because Michael respects Ryan's opinion.
我觉得她选瑞安是因为迈克尔很看重瑞安的意见。

877
00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:18.270
And if Ryan agrees, then Michael will believe it's cool.
如果瑞安表示赞同，迈克尔就会觉得这很酷。

878
00:42:18.590 --> 00:42:18.890
Right.
没错。

879
00:42:19.270 --> 00:42:22.390
You know, the scene ended with an extra beat.
你知道，那场戏结尾其实多了一小段。

880
00:42:22.570 --> 00:42:23.430
It's in the shooting draft.
在拍摄剧本里有。

881
00:42:23.530 --> 00:42:24.670
It didn't make it into the episode.
